Takes: {inputs}3A resource vial's tooltip!screen.alu.titleU{tier} ALU — {chips}/{max} chips working#ALU screen header!screen.alu.slotsCSlots 1–{max} work at this tier5Under the ALU's chip slots#screen.alu.inputsInputs�Graph node: the ALU's sides as sources (what their cables bring in)%screen.alu.outputsOutputs�Graph node: the ALU's sides as sinks (what goes out into their cables)'screen.alu.sleepingoffUA chip in a slot past the ALU tier's limit!screen.alu.emptyOPut programmed chips in the slots belowscreen.alu.busBus {side}�A bus node's title in the ALU graph (a side a digital cable reaches)screen.alu.help�
Inputs (left): what each side's cable brings in. Outputs (right): what goes out into it.
Drag from an output pin (right edge) to an input pin (left edge) to wire them — chip to chip stays inside the ALU.
Drag a wire off its input pin to move it, or into empty space to remove it. Drag a chip, or the In and Out panels, by its title.
Drag empty space to move the view; the wheel zooms it.
A side a Digital Cable reaches is a bus: wire into a channel's left pin to drive it, out of its right pin to read it; pull the bar at its bottom down for more channels.
Name a Redstone Port (right-click it) and its name shows on the side its cable reaches.ITooltip of the (i) in the ALU screen5screen.port.redstone_titlebblock.displayDisplay%block.display.desc�§7A 256×256 screen with a GPU, driven over a Digital Cable.
